<h1>5. Add Base Plugin Component (Updated for v10 / Angular 20 / Nx)</h1>

<p>This chapter describes how to add a custom plugin library to the Identity Manager Web Portal.
The plugin registers a dashboard tile that calls an API and displays results.</p>

<div class=3D"note">
<b>What changed from the original guide:</b>
<ul>
<li><span class=3D"strike">ng-package.dynamic.json</span> =E2=80=94 No longer needed</li>
<li><span class=3D"strike">tslint.json</span> =E2=80=94 Replaced by <code>.eslintrc.json</code></li>
<li><span class=3D"strike">"compilationMode": "partial"</span> =E2=80=94 Not needed for workspace libraries</li>
<li><span class=3D"strike">"enableIvy": true</span> =E2=80=94 Ivy is the only compiler in Angular 20</li>
<li><span class=3D"strike">imx-project.json</span> =E2=80=94 Replaced by <code>project.json</code> (Nx format)</li>
<li><span class=3D"strike">"dynamic" configuration in angular.json</span> =E2=80=94 Not needed; plugin is wired via <code>portal-dynamic-modules-import.service.ts</code></li>
<li><span class=3D"strike">Html_&lt;project-name&gt; folder on IIS</span> =E2=80=94 Not needed; plugin is bundled into the app at build time</li>
<li>Use <code>project.json</code> for Nx configuration instead of relying solely on <code>angular.json</code></li>
<li>The <code>imx-badge-tile</code> component (from <code>TilesModule</code> in <code>qer</code>) replaces the older <code>imx-tile</code></li>
</ul>
</div>

<h2>Overview</h2>

<p>A plugin library in the Identity Manager Web Portal consists of:</p>
<ol>
<li>A <b>library folder</b> under <code>projects/&lt;plugin-name&gt;/</code> with configuration files</li>
<li>A <b>module class</b> (e.g., <code>FrozenJobsPluginModule</code>) that bootstraps initialization</li>
<li>An <b>InitService</b> that registers components with the <code>ExtService</code></li>
<li>One or more <b>components</b> (e.g., a dashboard tile)</li>
<li><b>Workspace wiring</b>: entries in <code>angular.json</code>, <code>tsconfig.json</code>, and the dynamic import service</li>
</ol>

<h2>Phase 1: Scaffold the Library</h2>

<h3>Files to create under <code>projects/&lt;plugin-name&gt;/</code></h3>

<p>Copy these from the <code>rmb</code> or <code>rms</code> project and modify as described:</p>

<div class=3D"file-list">
<ul>
<li><code>ng-package.json</code></li>
<li><code>package.json</code></li>
<li><code>project.json</code> (Nx project definition)</li>
<li><code>tsconfig.lib.json</code></li>
<li><code>tsconfig.lib.prod.json</code></li>
<li><code>tsconfig.spec.json</code></li>
<li><code>karma.conf.js</code></li>
<li><code>.eslintrc.json</code></li>
<li><code>imx-plugin-config.json</code></li>
<li><code>src/public_api.ts</code></li>
<li><code>src/test.ts</code></li>
</ul>
</div>

<div class=3D"note">
In all files, replace <code>&lt;plugin-name&gt;</code> with your chosen library name.
In this example it is <b>"frozen-jobs-plugin"</b> and the module is <b>"FrozenJobsPluginModule"</b>.
</div>

<h3>Step 1: ng-package.json</h3>

<p>Controls ng-packagr output. Change <code>"dest"</code> to point to your library name:</p>

<pre>{
  "$schema": "../../node_modules/ng-packagr/ng-package.schema.json",
  "dest": "../../dist/frozen-jobs-plugin",
  "lib": {
    "entryFile": "src/public_api.ts",
    "styleIncludePaths": ["../../shared/scss"]
  }
}</pre>

<h3>Step 2: package.json</h3>

<pre>{
  "name": "frozen-jobs-plugin",
  "version": "10.0.0",
  "private": true
}</pre>

<h3>Step 3: project.json (Nx project definition)</h3>

<p>This replaces the old <code>imx-project.json</code>. Copy from <code>rmb/project.json</code> and replace all occurrences of "rmb" with your plugin name:</p>

<pre>{
  "$schema": "../../node_modules/nx/schemas/project-schema.json",
  "name": "frozen-jobs-plugin",
  "sourceRoot": "projects/frozen-jobs-plugin/src",
  "implicitDependencies": ["qer"],
  "projectType": "library",
  "prefix": "imx",
  "generators": {
    "@schematics/angular:component": {
      "style": "scss"
    }
  },
  "targets": {
    "build": {
      "executor": "@angular-devkit/build-angular:ng-packagr",
      "options": {
        "tsConfig": "projects/frozen-jobs-plugin/tsconfig.lib.json",
        "project": "projects/frozen-jobs-plugin/ng-package.json"
      },
      "configurations": {
        "production": {
          "tsConfig": "projects/frozen-jobs-plugin/tsconfig.lib.prod.json"
        },
        "development": {
          "tsConfig": "projects/frozen-jobs-plugin/tsconfig.lib.json"
        }
      },
      "outputs": ["{workspaceRoot}/dist/frozen-jobs-plugin"]
    },
    "test": {
      "executor": "@angular-devkit/build-angular:karma",
      "options": {
        "main": "projects/frozen-jobs-plugin/src/test.ts",
        "tsConfig": "projects/frozen-jobs-plugin/tsconfig.spec.json",
        "karmaConfig": "projects/frozen-jobs-plugin/karma.conf.js",
        "stylePreprocessorOptions": {
          "includePaths": [
            "./node_modules",
            "./node_modules/@elemental-ui/cadence-icon",
            "./node_modules/@elemental-ui/core",
            "./shared/scss"
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  }
}</pre>

<h3>Step 4: tsconfig.lib.json</h3>

<pre>{
  "extends": "../../tsconfig.json",
  "angularCompilerOptions": {
    "strictTemplates": true
  },
  "compilerOptions": {
    "outDir": "../../out-tsc/lib",
    "strictNullChecks": true,
    "declaration": true,
    "declarationMap": true,
    "sourceMap": true,
    "inlineSources": true,
    "types": []
  },
  "exclude": ["src/test.ts", "**/*.spec.ts"]
}</pre>

<h3>Step 5: tsconfig.lib.prod.json</h3>

<p>Simple =E2=80=94 no <code>compilationMode</code>, no <code>enableIvy</code>:</p>

<pre>{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.lib.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "declarationMap": false
  }
}</pre>

<h3>Step 6: imx-plugin-config.json</h3>

<p>This tells the portal which module to load. The <code>"Name"</code> must match your exported NgModule class name:</p>

<pre>{
  "qer-app-portal": [
    {
      "Container": "frozen-jobs-plugin",
      "Name": "FrozenJobsPluginModule"
    }
  ]
}</pre>

<h3>Step 7: src/public_api.ts</h3>

<pre>export { FrozenJobsPluginModule } from './lib/frozen-jobs-plugin.module';</pre>

<h2>Phase 2: Create Source Files</h2>

<h3>File: src/lib/frozen-jobs-plugin.module.ts</h3>

<p>The module class. Its constructor injects the InitService and calls <code>onInit()</code>:</p>

<pre>import { NgModule } from '@angular/core';
import { Routes, RouterModule } from '@angular/router';

import { TilesModule } from 'qer';
import { InitService } from './init.service';
import { FrozenJobsTileComponent } from './frozen-jobs-tile/frozen-jobs-tile.component';

const routes: Routes = [];

@NgModule({
  imports: [RouterModule.forChild(routes), TilesModule],
  declarations: [FrozenJobsTileComponent],
})
export class FrozenJobsPluginModule {
  constructor(private readonly initializer: InitService) {
    console.log('=F0=9F=94=A5 frozen-jobs-plugin loaded');
    this.initializer.onInit();
    console.log('=E2=96=B6=EF=B8=8F frozen-jobs-plugin initialized');
  }
}</pre>

<div class=3D"note">
<b>Key points:</b>
<ul>
<li>Import <code>TilesModule</code> from <code>qer</code> =E2=80=94 this provides the <code>&lt;imx-badge-tile&gt;</code> component</li>
<li>Declare your tile component in <code>declarations</code></li>
<li>The constructor pattern (inject service, call <code>onInit()</code>) is the same as all other plugins</li>
</ul>
</div>

<h3>File: src/lib/init.service.ts</h3>

<p>The init service registers your component as a dashboard tile using <code>ExtService</code>:</p>

<pre>import { Injectable } from '@angular/core';

import { ExtService } from 'qbm';
import { FrozenJobsTileComponent } from './frozen-jobs-tile/frozen-jobs-tile.component';

@Injectable({ providedIn: 'root' })
export class InitService {
  constructor(private readonly extService: ExtService) {}

  public onInit(): void {
    this.extService.register('Dashboard-SmallTiles', { instance: FrozenJobsTileComponent });
  }
}</pre>

<div class=3D"note">
<b>ExtService registration keys:</b>
<ul>
<li><code>'Dashboard-SmallTiles'</code> =E2=80=94 Badge tiles on the dashboard (uses <code>&lt;imx-badge-tile&gt;</code>)</li>
<li><code>'Dashboard-Tiles'</code> =E2=80=94 Large tiles on the dashboard (uses <code>&lt;imx-tile&gt;</code>)</li>
</ul>
</div>

<h3>File: src/lib/frozen-jobs-tile/frozen-jobs-tile.component.ts</h3>

<p>The tile component checks user group membership and calls an API:</p>

<pre>import { Component, OnInit } from '@angular/core';

import { imx_SessionService } from 'qbm';
import { UserModelService } from 'qer';

@Component({
  selector: 'imx-frozen-jobs-tile',
  templateUrl: './frozen-jobs-tile.component.html',
  standalone: false,
})
export class FrozenJobsTileComponent implements OnInit {
  public frozenJobsCount: number;
  public isAuthorized =3D false;
  public loading =3D true;

  constructor(
    private readonly session: imx_SessionService,
    private readonly userModelService: UserModelService,
  ) {}

  public async ngOnInit(): Promise&lt;void&gt; {
    try {
      const groups =3D await this.userModelService.getGroups();
      this.isAuthorized =3D groups.some(
        (g) =3D&gt; g.Name?.toUpperCase() =3D=3D=3D 'QER_4_OPERATIONSSUPPORT'
      );

      if (this.isAuthorized) {
        const result =3D await this.session.Client.opsupport_queue_frozenjobs_get(
          { PageSize: 20 }
        );
        this.frozenJobsCount =3D result?.TotalCount ?? 0;
      }
    } finally {
      this.loading =3D false;
    }
  }

  public onTileClick(): void {
    console.log('Frozen jobs tile clicked');
  }
}</pre>

<div class=3D"note">
<b>Permission checking pattern:</b><br>
Use <code>UserModelService.getGroups()</code> (from <code>qer</code>) which calls <code>GET /portal/usergroups</code>.
Check for group membership by name. This is the same pattern used by <code>isAuditor()</code> in the codebase.
</div>

<h3>File: src/lib/frozen-jobs-tile/frozen-jobs-tile.component.html</h3>

<pre>@if (isAuthorized &amp;&amp; !loading) {
  &lt;imx-badge-tile
    data-imx-identifier=3D"start-tile-frozen-jobs"
    [caption]=3D"'Frozen Jobs'"
    [tooltip]=3D"'Shows the number of frozen jobs in the process queue.'"
    [value]=3D"frozenJobsCount?.toString()"
    [identifier]=3D"'frozen-jobs'"
    (actionClick)=3D"onTileClick()"
  &gt;
  &lt;/imx-badge-tile&gt;
}</pre>

<div class=3D"note">
<b>Note:</b> The template uses Angular 17+ control flow syntax (<code>@if</code>) instead of the older <code>*ngIf</code> directive.
The <code>&lt;imx-badge-tile&gt;</code> component is from <code>TilesModule</code> (exported by <code>qer</code>).
</div>

<h2>Phase 3: Wire into Workspace</h2>

<p>Three workspace-level files must be modified:</p>

<h3>Step 1: IMXWEB/tsconfig.json</h3>

<p>Add path mappings in <code>compilerOptions.paths</code>:</p>

<pre>"frozen-jobs-plugin": ["dist/frozen-jobs-plugin"],
"frozen-jobs-plugin/*": ["dist/frozen-jobs-plugin/*"],</pre>

<h3>Step 2: IMXWEB/angular.json</h3>

<p>Add a new project entry. Copy the structure from any existing library (e.g., <code>rmb</code>) and replace names:</p>

<pre>"frozen-jobs-plugin": {
  "root": "projects/frozen-jobs-plugin",
  "sourceRoot": "projects/frozen-jobs-plugin/src",
  "projectType": "library",
  "prefix": "imx",
  "schematics": {
    "@schematics/angular:component": {
      "style": "scss"
    }
  },
  "architect": {
    "build": {
      "builder": "@angular-devkit/build-angular:ng-packagr",
      "options": {
        "tsConfig": "projects/frozen-jobs-plugin/tsconfig.lib.json",
        "project": "projects/frozen-jobs-plugin/ng-package.json"
      },
      "configurations": {
        "production": {
          "tsConfig": "projects/frozen-jobs-plugin/tsconfig.lib.prod.json"
        },
        "development": {
          "tsConfig": "projects/frozen-jobs-plugin/tsconfig.lib.json"
        }
      }
    },
    "test": { ... },
    "lint": { ... }
  }
}</pre>

<h3>Step 3: portal-dynamic-modules-import.service.ts</h3>

<p>File location: <code>projects/qer-app-portal/src/app/dynamic-import/portal-dynamic-modules-import.service.ts</code></p>

<p><b>Add the import at the top:</b></p>

<pre>import { FrozenJobsPluginModule } from "frozen-jobs-plugin";</pre>

<p><b>Add a case in the switch statement</b> (before <code>default</code>):</p>

<pre>case 'frozen-jobs-plugin':
  callback =3D async () =3D&gt; {
    await import('frozen-jobs-plugin');
    return [FrozenJobsPluginModule];
  };
  break;</pre>

<div class=3D"warning">
<b>Important:</b> The <code>case</code> value must exactly match the <code>"Container"</code> value in your <code>imx-plugin-config.json</code>.
</div>

<h2>Phase 4: Build and Verify</h2>

<h3>Build the library</h3>

<pre>npx nx build frozen-jobs-plugin --skip-nx-cache</pre>

<p>This also builds dependencies (<code>qbm</code>, <code>qer</code>) if not already built.</p>

<h3>Build the portal application</h3>

<pre>npx nx run qer-app-portal:build:production --skip-nx-cache</pre>

<p>Verify the plugin appears as a lazy chunk in the output:</p>

<pre>chunk-XXXXXXXX.js     | frozen-jobs-plugin | 128 bytes</pre>

<h3>Verify bundling</h3>

<pre>findstr /m "FrozenJobsPluginModule" dist\qer-app-portal\*.js</pre>

<h2>Phase 5: Deploy</h2>

<p>Copy the contents of <code>dist/qer-app-portal/</code> to your IIS deployment folder.
No separate <code>Html_&lt;plugin-name&gt;</code> folder is needed =E2=80=94 the plugin is bundled into the application.</p>

<div class=3D"warning">
<b>Nx cache:</b> If changes don't appear after rebuild, clear the cache with <code>npx nx reset</code> and rebuild with <code>--skip-nx-cache</code>.
</div>

